Found during k32. The warming fetch runs once; when it fails (stdio {"command": "false"}, an http url at a dead local port) the upstream goes back to 'stopped' with no error, and every tools/list gets 503 'is not ready yet' — the still-fetching meaning — until someone runs mcp-hub refresh. k32 fixed only the TLS case (fails at build time). Needs: a failed warming fetch either records the reason as 'failed' (with refresh clearing it) or retries with backoff; the 503 must not claim 'still fetching' when nothing is fetching.

2026-11-05 23:28 Started. Cause: MCP::Hub::_warm_upstream's catch only logs; every subclass start_p failure path sets state from its own {failed} crash-loop flag, which one failure never sets, so the upstream goes back to 'stopped' with error undef and _route_server's no-manifest branch answers 'not ready yet'. Same after a failing refresh (MCP::Hub::refresh_p). Plan: hub decides (only it knows a fetch is the warming fetch / a refresh of a never-listed upstream), upstream records via a new base method Upstream->fail(reason) that sets the subclasses' {failed} flag + error + state, so later async state changes (_on_close after a handshake-timeout kill) keep it failed and every refresh_p's _clear_failure undoes it. Writing red tests first.

